# An allowlist: `data/` is the owner's real database and their whole game archive, and
# nothing outside these paths is needed to build the image.
#
# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore` because the Dockerfile lives in docker/ while the build
# context is the repository root: BuildKit reads `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` beside the
# Dockerfile before it looks for one at the context root. Paths are context-relative.
*
!backend/
!web/
!docker/
!alembic.ini
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md

# `web/dist` is produced by the node stage inside the build. A host build copied in would
# be whatever was last run locally — possibly stale, possibly pointed at a dev backend.
web/dist/
web/node_modules/
web/.vite/
# Same reasoning for `web/.engine/`: it is a 15 MB download cache. The web stage fetches the
# net itself, from the checksum in `scripts/engine-assets.mjs`, so shipping the host's copy
# into the context would only make the build depend on what happens to be lying around.
web/.engine/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
